INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Why is drip tape spacing in chickpea cultivation of vital importance?</h2><p>The correct selection and layout of drip tape (Drip Tape) has become one of the main pillars of success in drip irrigation for sensitive crops such as chickpeas. Chickpea is a crop whose roots are shallower than those of many other legumes and which requires continuous moisture in the topsoil layer to prevent drought stress and fungal diseases. If the spacing between drip tapes or the distance of the tube from the roots is not observed, water will not be distributed uniformly, and energy and pumping costs will increase. Next, the technical standards for determining <strong>drip tape spacing for chickpea</strong> are explained in full detail.</p><h3>Quick introduction to the drip tape system</h3><p>Drip tape is a type of single-strip drip irrigation tube that is usually placed in the field permanently or temporarily and is collected after the end of the season. Unlike permanent drip tubing, drip tape is mobile, which is very practical for the cropping cycle of annual plants like chickpeas. Determining the exact spacing of these tapes relative to planting rows is the main key to uniform plant growth across the entire field.</p><h2>Drip tape spacing standards based on planting type</h2><p>The recommended drip tape spacing for chickpea cultivation depends entirely on the harvesting method and planting row layout. Generally, farmers deal with two planting methods: row planting and broadcast planting, but row planting is more suitable for drip irrigation.</p><h3>Tube offset from planting row (Offset)</h3><p>The most important parameter in drip tape spacing is the longitudinal distance between the tube and the seed sowing line. This distance should not be too small, as it may cause the tape to stick to the main root and lead to root asphyxiation. On the other hand, if the distance is too large, the wetting zone (Wetting Zone) will not reach the main root, and the plant will have to spend more energy to find water.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-نخود-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت نخود: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop chickpea</figcaption></figure><ul><li><strong>Standard spacing:</strong> For drip tapes with a standard emission rate, a distance of 10 to 15 centimeters from the center of the planting row is ideal.</li><li><strong>Tape in the middle of the row:</strong> In some advanced systems, two tapes are laid 30 centimeters apart from the center of the row to ensure moisture coverage on both sides of the root.</li></ul><h3>Longitudinal spacing between tapes in the direction of field length</h3><p>If permanent tapes with limited length are used, the tape connection spacing must be at least 50 centimeters to ensure uniform water distribution. However, if the spacing refers to the layout of parallel tapes, this depends on the Bed Width intended.</p><h3>Impact of emission rate on drip tape spacing</h3><p>The Flow Rate, measured in centimeters per hour, directly impacts the allowable Emitter Spacing. For chickpea cultivation, emitters spaced 30 to 40 cm apart are recommended. If emitters are placed closer together, the wetting zone forms faster, allowing for shorter drip tape lengths.</p><h2></h2><h2>Practical Guide for Drip Tape Layout in Chickpea Fields</h2><p>In practice, you must draw a precise field map before starting irrigation. A common error is a mismatch between drip tape length and plot length, which causes dry spots at the tape end. To correct this, use pressure regulators on the lateral line ends to ensure uniform water flow.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-نخود-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت نخود: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>drip tape spacing row layout crop chickpea</figcaption></figure><h3>Checking Planting Depth and Vertical Spacing</h3><p>Chickpea drip tape spacing involves more than just horizontal distance. The burial depth or surface placement of the tape is also critical. For chickpeas, place the tape on the surface or semi-buried (about 5 cm). Deeper burial alters soil moisture dynamics and may fail to deliver sufficient moisture to the soil surface where the main chickpea stem grows.</p><ul><li><strong>Bedding:</strong> If using raised beds for chickpea planting, the drip tape should be positioned 20 to 25 cm from the bed crest to ensure roots establish in the bed edge where moisture levels are higher.</li><li><strong>Terrace cultivation:</strong> In sloped areas, drip tape spacing should not follow the terrain gradient to prevent mechanical stress on the tape.</li></ul><h3>Proper Connection and Clog Prevention</h3><p>Since leguminous crops like chickpea are susceptible to fungal infections, irrigation system hygiene is maintained through appropriate spacing and flow rates. Using suitable filters at the drip tape inlet increases emitter lifespan.</p><h2></h2><h2>Analogies with Other Crops and Supplementary Notes</h2><p>Adhering to drip irrigation principles in chickpea cultivation follows the same standards used for other major crops such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/miqdori-tuxmi-javori-donador-dar-yak-gektar/">how to plant barley and the seed rate per hectare</a> or even in high-yield systems such as soybean irrigation. The primary difference lies in root depth and moisture requirements. While soybean has deeper roots, chickpea requires a surface wetting zone. Additionally, familiarity with general water resource management principles across various crops, such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/miqdori-tuxmi-lobiya-sabz-dar-yak-gektar-rahnamoi-kisht/">green bean irrigation guidelines</a> can provide a broader perspective.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/فاصله-نوار-تیپ-در-کشت-نخود-استانداردهای-توصیهشده-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="فاصله نوار تیپ در کشت نخود: استانداردهای توصیه‌شده - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Chickpea drip tape spacing row layout crop</figcaption></figure><p>One common mistake is failing to adjust the drip tape spacing to the soil type. In sandy soils, the spacing between emitters should be shorter (e.g., 25 cm) because vertical infiltration is faster, whereas 40 cm spacing is more suitable for clay soils. This adjustment directly impacts the final yield per hectare and can determine your profitability.</p><h2></h2><h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) about Chickpea Drip Tape Spacing</h2><ol><li><strong>Can I place the drip tape in the center of the chickpea planting row?</strong><br>Yes, if you use tapes with high discharge rates, placement in the center or on both sides at a distance of 10-15 cm from the planting line is permitted and even recommended. This ensures moisture reaches the early root establishment zone more quickly.</li><li><strong>What impact does drip tape length have on energy consumption?</strong><br>The longer a lateral line is, the greater the pressure drop. If the distance between parallel tapes is large, forcing the use of shorter main lines, installation and main piping costs decrease, but you must pay attention to pressure loss at the end of the tape.</li><li><strong>What is the best time to replace old drip tape in chickpea cultivation?</strong><br>Always before planting. Since chickpeas establish roots quickly, worn-out tape causes clogging and results in the loss of the critical window for initial irrigation.</li></ol><h3>Safety Warnings for Drip Tape Spacing Installation</h3><ul><li>Never use drip tape in direct proximity to applied soil fumigants; maintain a safe distance from the fumigation area.</li><li>In heavy soils, do not let the chickpea drip tape spacing cross the plowing lines to prevent tape abrasion.</li></ul><h2>Conclusion and Final Recommendations</h2><p>Adhering to drip tape spacing standards in chickpea cultivation can increase water savings by up to 30% and promote uniform plant growth. The key is matching the emitter spacing to the soil infiltration depth and the planting system. It is recommended to request the hydraulic performance chart for your specific tape from the manufacturer before purchasing, to select the optimal spacing and discharge rate based on your field length. Proper implementation of this guide is an effective step toward modern and sustainable agriculture.</p>\n<p><strong>Related Articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%d9%be%d9%86%d8%a8%d9%87-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Cotton Yield Per Hectare: A Comprehensive Guide for Farmers</a>, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%AA%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%DB%8C%DA%A9%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%87-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">D985D982D8AFD8A7D8B1 D8A8D8B0D8B1 D8AAD8B1DB8CD8AADB8CDAA9D8A7D984D987 D8AFD8B1 D987DAA9D8AAD8A7D8B1</a></p>','Drip Tape Spacing for Chickpea: Recommended Standards and Irrigation Considerations','This article provides a detailed examination of drip line spacing standards for chickpea cultivation. Correctly determining these intervals is essential for optimizing water use and increasing crop yield.','publish','closed','closed','drip-tape-spacing-chickpea-irrigation-standards',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
